ters of Reference\nOfficial Test Scores (GRE, GMAT, & English Language Proficiency)\nTest Preparation\nAdditional Admissions Materials\nInternational Applicants\nEnglish Language Proficiency Requirements\nForeign Credential Evaluation Services\nI-20 Requirements\nVisa Guidelines for International Graduate Enrollment\nPrograms & Deadlines\nThe Application Process\nApplication Checklist\nApply Now\nAfter You Apply\nCheck Application Status\nSteps to Update/Defer Your Entry Term\nSteps After Admission\nNew Student Orientations\nAdmission Decisions\nTuition & Funding\nTuition & Fees\nWays to Fund Graduate School\nGraduate Fellowships\nGraduate Assistantships\nRecent Graduate Assistantship Openings\nMcNair Graduate Scholars Program\nTeacher Tuition Incentive Program\nFinancial Aid\nCampus & Community\nHousing\nParking\nVisit Campus\nRequest Information\nCurrent Students\nAdmitted Students\nAcademic Calendar\nGraduate Catalog\nGraduation Guide\nGraduate School Forms\nAwards & Funding\nAppeals\nResources\nWriting Support\nDissertation Boot Camp\nResearch Resources\nResearch\nNCFDD Resources\nProfessional Advancement\nThree Minute Thesis Form\nPersonal Finance Planning\nStudent Organizations\nGraduate Student Organization\nGrad in Focus - Monthly Newsletters\nGraduate Student Appreciation Week\nGraduate Assistantship Handbook\nAbout Us\nA Message from the Dean\nMeet Our Staff\nGraduate Faculty\nFunding Your Students\nEngaging Constructively and Productively with Graduate Students\nJoin the Graduate Faculty\nCurrent Graduate Faculty\nCollege of the Arts\nB. I. Moody III College of Business Administration\nCollege of Education and Human Development\nCollege of Engineering\nCollege of Liberal Arts\nCollege of Nursing and Health Sciences\nRay P. Authement College of Sciences\nUniversity Guidelines\nCollege Criteria\nGraduate Faculty Membership Application\nGraduate Council\nGraduate Council Handbook\nGraduate Council Standing Committees\nGraduate Council Minutes & Agendas\nGraduate School Blog\nGraduate School News & Stories\nGraduate School Feedback\nContact Us\nGraduate assistantships can provide financial support as well as professional experience for your future career.\nMost graduate assistantships\u2014whether teaching, research, or administration focused\u2014are awarded on a competitive basis, with academic merit being the primary consideration.\nTypically, these assistantships are awarded by individual graduate programs and research faculty members or centers, but many administrative offices on campus also hire graduate assistants.\nHow to Find Assistantships\nContact your graduate coordinator directly to find out about teaching and research assistantships available in your program of study.\nTo find out about assistantships outside of your graduate program:\nContact individual offices and research centers on campus\nFollow the UL Lafayette Grad School Facebook page for GA Opening announcements\nCheck out postings on the Office of Career Services website.\nImportant Guidelines & Policies\nGraduate assistantships\u2014including Graduate Teaching Assistantships (GTA), Graduate Research Assistantships (GRA), and Graduate Assistantships (GA)\u2014are governed by policies outlined in the University Catalog.\nIndividual graduate programs also have guidelines and resources available for GTAs, GRAs, and GAs. Contact your graduate coordinator for more information.\nLearn more about paying for graduate school\nHow to Apply\nTo ensure consideration for assistantship funding all required application materials must be received by the priority assistantship deadline for the semester in which you are applying.\nApplication Form\nComplete the Assistantship Application and upload it to your application portal or deliver it in person.\nNov. 1\nSpring Priority Deadline\nSubmit all application materials by Nov 1 to ensure consideration for an assistantship in the next Spring semester.\nMarch 1\nFall Priority Deadline\nSubmit all application materials by March 1 to ensure consideration for an assistantship in the next Fall semester.\nIndividual graduate degree programs may adhere to different program deadlines. Please contact your graduate coordinator directly for deadline information.\nRequest Information\nVisit Campus\nApply\n337-482-6965\ngradschool@louisiana.edu\nMartin Hall, Suite 332\n104 University Circle\nLafayette, LA 70503\nGraduate Programs\nAdmissions\nBefore You Apply\nApply Now\nAfter You Apply\nTuition & Funding\nTuition & Fees\nWays to Fund Graduate School\nGraduate Fellowships\nGraduate Assistantships\nRecent Graduate Assistantship Openings\nMcNair Graduate Scholars Program\nTeacher Tuition Incentive Program\nFinancial Aid\nCampus & Community\nRequest Information\nCurrent Students\nResources\nAbout Us\nFacebook\nX\nInstagram\n\u00a9 University of Louisiana at Lafayette. All rights reserved.", "links": [["Skip to main site navigation", "https://louisiana.edu/graduateschool/admissions/tuition-funding/funding-opportunities/graduate-assistantships#main-menu"], ["Skip to main content", "https://louisiana.edu/graduateschool/admissions/tuition-funding/funding-opportunities/graduate-assistantships#main-content"], ["Back to Louisiana.edu", "https://louisiana.edu/"], ["", "https://louisiana.edu/graduateschool"], ["Back to Louisiana.edu", "https://louisiana.edu/"], ["", "https://louisiana.edu/graduateschool"], ["Graduate Programs", "https://louisiana.edu/graduateschool/graduate-programs"], ["Graduate Programs", "https://louisiana.edu/graduateschool/graduate-programs"], ["All Programs", "https://louisiana.edu/graduateschool/graduate-programs/all-programs"], ["Master's Degrees", "https://louisiana.edu/graduateschool/graduate-programs/masters-degrees"], ["Doctoral Degrees", "https://louisiana.edu/graduateschool/graduate-programs/doctoral-degrees"], ["Graduate Certificates", "https://louisiana.edu/graduateschool/graduate-programs/graduate-certificates"], ["Non-Degree Programs", "https://louisiana.edu/graduate